Structural modeling connects pre-defined component modules using interconnecting nets (`wire`), reflecting the physical schematic hierarchy.

Code Example:
```verilog
module full_adder_struct (
    input wire a, b, cin,
    output wire sum, cout
);
    wire s1, c1, c2;

    // Instantiate HA1 and HA2
    half_adder ha1 (.a(a), .b(b), .sum(s1), .cout(c1));
    half_adder ha2 (.a(s1), .b(cin), .sum(sum), .cout(c2));

    // OR gate primitive for final carry
    or (cout, c1, c2);
endmodule
```
